#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.89pt, 790.176pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.824pt, 84pt, "Generation, Annihilation and Flow of Structural Information in Ultrasonic ")
  #line-at(217.73pt, 101.42pt, "Nondestructive Evaluation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165.02pt, 126.74pt, "Dr. Frank Schubert, Fraunhofer IKTS, Dresden ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 171.86pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 194.78pt, "Non-destructive testing using ultrasound is based on the interaction of sound waves with the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 209.66pt, "object being tested and any defects it may contain. The aim is to extract as much information ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 224.54pt, "as possible about the object and its defects from the scattered wave field. In this paper, the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 239.42pt, "concept of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.06pt, 239.42pt, "information")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.82pt, 239.42pt, " in the context of ultrasonic testing is formalized and quantified physi-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 254.3pt, "cally for the first time. To this end, a balance equation for information is derived, analogous to ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 269.18pt, "Poynting's theorem for elastic energy. Various examples demonstrate how structural infor-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 284.09pt, "mation is generated and annihilated within a component and along which pathways it travels ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 298.97pt, "from the defect to the sensor. Subsequently, the significance and potential of this new infor-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 313.85pt, "mation concept for practical ultrasonic testing, structural health monitoring, numerical simula-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 328.85pt, "tion, and machine learning are discussed. Finally, similarities and differences to mathematical ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 343.73pt, "Shannon information and statistical Fisher information are highlighted. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.944pt, 389.45pt, "1.")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 389.45pt, "Introduction and Motivation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 412.37pt, "The American mathematician and electrical engineer Claude E. Shannon (1916–2001) laid the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 427.25pt, "foundations for a systematic and quantifiable concept of information with his groundbreaking ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 442.13pt, "publication ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.14pt, 442.13pt, "A Mathematical Theory of Communication")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(339.67pt, 442.13pt, " [1] in 1948, thus paving the way for ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 457.01pt, "modern information and communication technology. Terms like ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.35pt, 457.01pt, "bits")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(397.75pt, 457.01pt, " and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.55pt, 457.01pt, "bytes")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.03pt, 457.01pt, " are a direct con-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 471.91pt, "sequence of this work and have entered both scientific and general usage. Against this back-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 486.79pt, "drop, it is surprising that the term ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(236.57pt, 486.79pt, "information")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.33pt, 486.79pt, " in non-destructive evaluation (NDE) and struc-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 501.67pt, "tural health monitoring (SHM) has so far only been used colloquially, and that there is no phys-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 516.67pt, "ically formalized and quantifiable theory for it. NDE is fundamentally based on the interaction ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 531.55pt, "of physical fields with the object under investigation and any defects it may contain. The aim ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 546.43pt, "is to extract as much information as possible about the component and its defects from the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 561.31pt, "altered or scattered field. The concept of information in NDE is therefore so fundamental that ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 576.19pt, "a formalized theory could lead to groundbreaking new insights and systematic improvements ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 591.07pt, "in testing systems, inspection setups, and evaluation methods. This paper presents a first attempt ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 605.95pt, "at developing such a theory using ultrasonic testing as an example. However, the basic concept ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 620.83pt, "can, in principle, be applied to many other NDE and SHM methods, particularly elastodynamic ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 635.71pt, "and acoustic methods, electromagnetic and optical methods, eddy current testing, and thermo-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 650.59pt, "graphy, to name just a few important examples. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 673.54pt, "Section 2 begins by discussing various sensible requirements and criteria for an information ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 688.42pt, "measure suitable for ultrasonic NDE. Section 3 then examines in detail the significance of sys-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 703.3pt, "tem changes and differential wave fields in a simplified, one-dimensional model using numer-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 718.18pt, "ical wave field simulations. Section 4 formalizes the identified information measure, culminat-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 733.18pt, "ing in a one-dimensional balance equation for structural information. In this context, the con-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 748.056pt, "cepts of information density, information flow, and information sources and sinks are intro-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 762.936pt, "duced, and the similarities and differences to Poynting's theorem for elastic energy are ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.89pt, 790.176pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 82.08pt, "discussed. Section 5 verifies the identified information quantities using selected simulations. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 96.98pt, "Section 6 demonstrates the significance of information at the sensor location and in the time ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 111.86pt, "signal detected, respectively. Here, the new concept of ‘change bits’, or shortly, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(455.71pt, 111.86pt, "Cbits")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.18pt, 111.86pt, ", is intro-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 126.74pt, "duced as a quantitative absolute unit of information. Finally, Section 7 discusses the relevance ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 141.62pt, "of the new information measure for ultrasonic NDE, SHM, machine learning, and numerical ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 156.5pt, "simulation. Section 8 addresses similarities and differences to Shannon information from math-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 171.38pt, "ematical information theory and Fisher information from statistics. The article concludes with ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 186.26pt, "a summary and outlook in Section 9. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.944pt, 232.1pt, "2.")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 232.1pt, "Requirements for a Suitable Information Measure  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 255.02pt, "The better the interaction process between ultrasound waves excited by the probe and the de-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 269.9pt, "fects present in the component is understood, the more optimally the testing system can be ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 284.81pt, "configured and the more effectively the time signals detected by the sensor can be evaluated. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 299.69pt, "For many years, numerical simulations have been used to elucidate this interaction, either in ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 314.57pt, "the form of commercially available software packages or in the form of individual in-house ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 329.45pt, "developments by various research groups. All numerical methods have individual advantages ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 344.33pt, "and disadvantages and are based on different mathematical-numerical approaches, but they es-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 359.21pt, "sentially solve the same fundamental physical equations describing wave propagation, such as ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 374.21pt, "the wave equation, on a spatiotemporal surface or space grid. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 397.01pt, "Figure 1 shows an example of the interaction of a wave field emitted by an ultrasonic transducer ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 411.89pt, "with an elastic inclusion embedded in a homogeneous isotropic matrix medium, calculated us-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 426.77pt, "ing the author's EFIT simulation tool [2]. Due to the numerous diffraction and mode conversion ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 441.77pt, "effects, as well as the slight inclination of the elliptical inclusion, a very complex, asymmetric ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 456.65pt, "scattered field results, consisting of various longitudinal and transverse wave components. The ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 471.55pt, "scattered field depends on various parameters of the inclusion, such as its position, size, shape ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 486.43pt, "and orientation, its material properties, and - at a later stage - also on the position and shape of ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 501.31pt, "the component's back wall or boundaries (via secondary interactions). ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 524.23pt, "In a sense, the wave field shown in Figure 1 therefore contains ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(373.03pt, 524.23pt, "structural information")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.1pt, 524.23pt, " about all ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 539.11pt, "these parameters, albeit in a cumulative, non-separable form. Based on the individual simula-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 553.99pt, "tion, it is not possible to determine precisely where in the wave field the information, e.g., about ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 568.87pt, "the orientation of the scatterer or its material properties, is stored and how it propagates to a ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 583.75pt, "sensor. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 606.67pt, "From the considerations above, a first important requirement for the information measure to be ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 621.55pt, "found can be formulated: ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 644.47pt, "1)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 644.47pt, "The generation and flow of information should be describable for each structural pa-")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 659.38pt, "rameter of the system individually, that is, separately from one another. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 682.3pt, "Further meaningful requirements arise directly from the separation and characterization of the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 697.18pt, "incident and scattered fields (see Figure 1): ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 719.98pt, "2)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 719.98pt, "Since the information about the individual structural parameters is only encoded in the ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 734.98pt, "scattered wave field, the incident wave field generated by the probe cannot carry any ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 749.856pt, "information as long as it has not interacted with any scatterer (see sub-figure 1 in Fig. 1). ")
]

