  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.94pt, 82.08pt, "different materials, and possibly also the volume of the scatterer, can serve as sources ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 96.98pt, "of information (see sub-figure 2 in Figure 1). ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 111.86pt, "5)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 111.86pt, "It is plausible to assume that information is coupled to the propagation of the scattered ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 126.74pt, "waves, i.e., that the latter serve as carriers of the information. Therefore, information ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 141.62pt, "should also propagate at the speed of the respective wave. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 164.54pt, "Further fundamental requirements for the information measure, which is yet to be defined, can ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 179.42pt, "be derived from the separate investigation of reflected and transmitted wave components. For ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 194.3pt, "this purpose, we consider the simplified one-dimensional model with triple layering shown in ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 209.18pt, "Figure 2.  ")
