  #line-at(70.944pt, 210.38pt, "If, in this model, we are interested in the depth (or position) of the layer, i.e., the distance be-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 225.26pt, "tween the excitation probe (left boundary of the model) and the left or right layer boundary as ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 240.14pt, "a structural parameter, it becomes clear that only the two reflected waves from the left and right ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 255.02pt, "layer boundaries can carry information about the depth, not the transmitted wave. As long as ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 269.9pt, "the second receiving probe at the right boundary of the model is sufficiently far from the layer ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 284.81pt, "(to avoid reflections between the two), the detected transmitted wave field in this one-dimen-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 299.81pt, "sional three-layer case remains independent of the layer's position and therefore cannot carry ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 314.69pt, "any information about it. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 337.49pt, "This changes, however, if we shift the second (right) layer boundary to the right edge of the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 352.37pt, "model (Figure 3). In this two-layer case, the depth (or position) of the layer (more precisely: of ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 367.37pt, "the remaining left layer boundary) can be determined from the effective travel time of the trans-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 382.25pt, "mitted wave, provided we assume the sound velocities of the matrix and the layer are known. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 397.13pt, "In this case, the information about the layer position must also be encoded in the transmitted ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 412.01pt, "wave and must have already been generated at the (only existing) left layer boundary, since the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 426.89pt, "influence of the sound velocity of the layer on the final travel time starts there. Since the left ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 441.77pt, "layer boundary is also present in the three-layer case, it follows that the position information ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 456.65pt, "generated there must be lost again in the forward-propagating wave in the three-layer system ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 471.55pt, "but must be preserved in the two-layer case. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 494.47pt, "The above considerations lead us to the final requirements for our information measure for now: ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 517.39pt, "6)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 517.39pt, "For individual waves, such as the forward wave in Figure 2 and Figure 3, there must be ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 532.27pt, "local sinks of information (e.g., the right layer boundary) in addition to information ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 547.15pt, "sources (here, the left layer boundary), where previously generated information is either ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 562.03pt, "annihilated or at least removed from this wave. ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 576.91pt, "7)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 576.91pt, "Point 6, together with requirement 4, suggests that, unlike (elastic) energy, information ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 591.79pt, "is not a globally conserved physical quantity of the system under consideration, but can ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 606.67pt, "apparently only be conserved between two interactions. As soon as another interaction ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 621.55pt, "occurs, the information can be lost and/or new information can be generated. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 644.47pt, "An information measure suitable for ultrasonic NDE should possess at least the seven properties ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 659.38pt, "formulated in this section in order to be practically meaningful and consistent in its application. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 674.26pt, "In the next section, we will present a promising candidate and examine the extent to which it ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 689.14pt, "fulfills requirements 1-7. ")
]

