  #line-at(177.5pt, 240.14pt, "𝐷1−")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(195.02pt, 237.74pt, ". We thus shift the two layer boundaries of the original model by one ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 252.98pt, "grid cell to the right and left, respectively, obtaining two new model systems, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.31pt, 252.98pt, "𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(456.19pt, 255.38pt, "𝐷1+")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(477.22pt, 252.98pt, "and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.1pt, 252.98pt, "𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(503.98pt, 255.38pt, "𝐷1−")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.62pt, 252.98pt, ", ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 268.1pt, "whose results will differ only slightly from the original model ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(371.47pt, 268.1pt, "𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.35pt, 270.5pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(382.75pt, 268.1pt, ", since the EFIT grid cells are ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 283.01pt, "significantly smaller than the wavelengths predominant in the broadband signal. Nevertheless, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 297.89pt, "there are differences, which can be most easily represented by the difference wave field, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 313.13pt, "𝑊(𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.744pt, 315.53pt, "𝐷1+")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.983pt, 315.53pt, " −𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.42pt, 315.53pt, "𝐷1−")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.18pt, 312.65pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(154.1pt, 313.13pt, ". In Figure")
  #line-at(205.73pt, 313.13pt, "5, this difference wave field with respect to the layer position (mid-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 328.37pt, "dle column) is compared with the wave field of the original model, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.71pt, 328.37pt, "𝑊(𝑆")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(415.51pt, 330.77pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.91pt, 328.37pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(425.83pt, 328.37pt, " (left column). In the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 343.13pt, "latter, the maximum amplitude of the excitation signal is normalized to one. In this example, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 358.01pt, "the amplitudes of the difference waves are all less than 2%. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 381.29pt, "The first three images up to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.45pt, 381.29pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.73pt, 381.29pt, " 6.53 µs show the moment shortly before, during, and after the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 396.05pt, "interaction with the left layer boundary. The difference wave field with respect to position is ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 411.41pt, "initially zero (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(139.58pt, 411.41pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(156.86pt, 411.41pt, " 4.16 µs) and is only generated at the moment of interaction at the left layer ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 426.53pt, "boundary (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.86pt, 426.53pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.14pt, 426.53pt, " 5.35 µs). After the interaction, a difference wave propagates in both the back-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 441.41pt, "ward and forward directions, with the forward wave exhibiting a significantly smaller amplitude ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 456.65pt, "and a different phase in the direction of propagation within the layer (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(407.11pt, 456.65pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(424.39pt, 456.65pt, " 6.53 µs). The wave-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 471.43pt, "form of the difference field differs significantly from that of the particle velocity in the initial ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 486.31pt, "model and resembles its spatial derivative. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 509.59pt, "The following three images, from")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(235.37pt, 509.59pt, " 𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(256.01pt, 509.59pt, " 7.52 µs to")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(309.17pt, 509.59pt, " 𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(329.57pt, 509.59pt, " 12.08 µs, show the interaction with the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 524.47pt, "right layer boundary. The newly generated difference wave field is radiated exclusively in the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 539.71pt, "backward direction, not in the forward direction (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.57pt, 539.71pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(325.85pt, 539.71pt, " 7.52 µs and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(388.03pt, 539.71pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.31pt, 539.71pt, " 8.91 µs). The difference ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 554.47pt, "wave initially present, originating from the left layer boundary, therefore disappears in the for-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 569.35pt, "ward direction. The new, backward-directed difference wave exhibits a higher amplitude within ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 584.59pt, "the layer than before the interaction with the right layer boundary (cf.")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(418.99pt, 584.59pt, " 𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.23pt, 584.59pt, " 6.53 µs and")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(503.26pt, 584.59pt, " 𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 599.47pt, "8.91 µs). After passing through the layer, both the difference wave from the left and the one ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 614.71pt, "from the right layer boundary again exhibit comparable amplitudes in the matrix medium (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(507.22pt, 614.71pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 629.47pt, "12.08 µs). However, both waves have opposite phase relationships in the direction of propaga-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 644.47pt, "tion, apparently as a result of wave reflection at the acoustically soft (right layer boundary) and ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 659.38pt, "acoustically hard (left layer boundary) transition. It is also worth noting that the difference wave ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 674.26pt, "originating at the left layer boundary and propagating in the reverse direction is reflected at the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 689.14pt, "left stress-free model boundary without a phase shift, analogous to the particle velocity in the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 704.02pt, "original model. ")
]

