// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.13pt, 790.176pt, "13 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 82.08pt, "also be the source of information. The difference wave fields thus arise from the difference ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 96.98pt, "between the pure scattered waves of the two variations and are therefore only generated during ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 111.86pt, "the interaction of the incident wave field with the scatterer(s) (requirement 4). Not only can the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 126.74pt, "scattering interfaces between two different materials act as sources of information, but also the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 141.62pt, "volume of the scatterer itself, as in the considered case of the change in sound velocity from ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 156.5pt, "Figure 8 (right column). This, too, is plausible and obvious. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 179.42pt, "We have further observed that all occurring difference waves are always correlated with a wave ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 194.3pt, "of the original model and therefore propagate at its speed (requirement 5). Each difference wave ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 209.18pt, "is always coupled to an original wave as the carrier of information, but conversely, not every ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 224.06pt, "original wave is coupled to a difference wave. Thus, during the change in position shown in ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 238.94pt, "Figure 5, the difference wave originating at the left layer boundary and propagating forward is ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 253.94pt, "suppressed at the right layer boundary, so that no information is transferred into the transmitted ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 268.82pt, "wave. For such individual waves (here the forward wave), there can therefore apparently be ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 283.73pt, "effective sinks of information in addition to sources (requirement 6). However, since in this ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 298.61pt, "example the interaction with the right layer boundary results in more information overall than ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 313.49pt, "originally came from the left layer boundary (the reflected difference wave in the layer is larger ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 328.37pt, "than the incoming difference wave in the forward direction), it remains initially unclear whether ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 343.25pt, "there can also be global sinks of information where information is actually annihilated. The ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 358.13pt, "examples considered so far in the homogeneous and lossless model do not provide direct evi-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 373.01pt, "dence for this. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 395.93pt, "However, the examples clearly show that difference waves can, in principle, arise during any ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 410.81pt, "scattering process (e.g., during the thickness change in Figure 5  at both layer boundaries). This ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 425.69pt, "demonstrates that, unlike (elastic) energy, information is generally ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.15pt, 425.69pt, "not")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(418.51pt, 425.69pt, " a globally conserved ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 440.57pt, "quantity of the system under consideration, but can apparently only be conserved between two ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 455.45pt, "interactions. Thus, difference wave fields also fulfill requirement 7 for the information measure ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 470.47pt, "to be found. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 493.27pt, "In the following section, we supplement and formalize our identified information measure and ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 508.15pt, "derive a specific balance equation for it. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.944pt, 553.99pt, "4.")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 553.99pt, "Formalization of Information Concept and Balance Equations in 1-D ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 576.91pt, "Despite the obvious suitability of difference wave fields as a measure of information, four for-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 591.79pt, "mal problems still need to be resolved. These can be expressed as further requirements 8-11, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 606.67pt, "thus supplementing the listing 1-7 from Section 2. ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 629.95pt, "8)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 629.95pt, "The information must be preserved even in the limiting case of vanishing changes ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.26pt, 629.95pt, "∆𝑃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.14pt, 629.95pt, "; ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 645.07pt, "otherwise, no information could be assigned to the initial wave field (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.95pt, 645.07pt, "∆𝑃→0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(479.26pt, 645.07pt, "). ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 659.98pt, "9)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 659.98pt, "The information should not be described by a signed quantity (such as particle velocity) ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 674.86pt, "that can be positive or negative, but rather, like energy, should only have positive values. ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 689.74pt, "10)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 689.74pt, "In a linear, attenuation- and noise-free system, the information must not depend on the ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 704.62pt, "amplitude of the excitation signal but must be preserved under simple scaling of the ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 719.5pt, "excitation. ")
  #line-at(88.944pt, 734.38pt, "11)")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 734.38pt, "The information should be physically dimensionless and, as information density relative ")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 749.496pt, "to the volume ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(175.94pt, 749.496pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(183.86pt, 749.496pt, ", have the physical dimension ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(329.21pt, 749.496pt, "1")
  #line-at(342.43pt, 749.496pt, "𝑉")
  #line-at(335.83pt, 749.016pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(350.35pt, 749.496pt, ". ")
]

