  #line-at(407.47pt, 417.29pt, ", respectively, explicitly ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 432.05pt, "illustrate the limitations of the theory presented here. When formulating the new balance equa-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 447.41pt, "tion(s), we started with the partial derivative with respect to only one system parameter ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(494.38pt, 447.41pt, "𝑃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(502.06pt, 447.41pt, " (see ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 462.17pt, "equations (16) und (17)). This means that the derived expressions can only describe cases in ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 477.07pt, "which one parameter changes independently of the others. If two or more parameters change ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 491.95pt, "simultaneously and independently, this can no longer be adequately captured by the equations. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 507.19pt, "The two material quantities ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.53pt, 507.19pt, "𝜌")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.25pt, 507.19pt, "and")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(234.29pt, 507.19pt, "𝜆+ 2𝜇")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(268.61pt, 507.19pt, "  are elementary components of the model description ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 522.07pt, "and thus belong to the set of possible material-related system parameters. Therefore, the same ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 536.95pt, "applies to them as stated above: only one of the two quantities can change independently, but ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 551.83pt, "not both at the same time. A conditional change between these two material properties is al-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 566.71pt, "lowed but must then be induced by a constant speed of sound, assumed to be known, according ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 582.07pt, "to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
