  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 82.08pt, "As the wave reflected at the right layer boundary passes through the left layer boundary, its ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 96.98pt, "maximum amplitude increases. However, the width of the transmitted pulse also decreases. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 111.86pt, "Additionally, by reflection another small information density wave in the forward direction is ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 126.98pt, "generated (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.58pt, 126.98pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.86pt, 126.98pt, " 12.08 µs). ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 149.9pt, "The information flux vector in the middle column of Figure 21 exhibits the same fundamental ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 164.78pt, "behavior as the information density, with the signs of the waves also correctly indicating their ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 179.66pt, "respective directions of propagation (positive sign = direction of propagation to the right, neg-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 194.66pt, "ative sign = direction of propagation to the left). ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 217.46pt, "The cumulative source terms of information in the right-hand column of Figure 21 show only ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 232.34pt, "contributions at the two layer boundaries, very similar to the case of the geometric parameters ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 247.34pt, "from Sections 5.2 and 5.3. Their time history, shown in Figure 22, reveals two temporally sep-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 262.22pt, "arated, positive contributions from the left layer boundary and one negative contribution from ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 277.13pt, "the right layer boundary. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 460.97pt, "Figure 22: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.18pt, 460.97pt, "Normalized time-dependent representation of the source term appearing in the model at the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 474.67pt, "left (left) and right layer boundary (right). Both curves are normalized to the maximum of the left source ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 488.35pt, "term. The vertical dashed lines serve as a guide and represent the theoretical arrival times of the signal ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 502.15pt, "at the left layer boundary (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(189.26pt, 502.15pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(205.13pt, 502.15pt, " 5.00 µs), at the right layer boundary (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.43pt, 502.15pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(391.27pt, 502.15pt, " 7.22 µs), and again at the left ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 516.07pt, "layer boundary (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(144.74pt, 516.07pt, "𝑡=")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(160.58pt, 516.07pt, " 9.45 µs). The source contribution at the right layer boundary is negative, thus this ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 529.75pt, "layer boundary acts as a sink of information.   ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 552.31pt, "Figure 23 again shows the temporal evolution of the information present in the model, divided ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 567.19pt, "into the kinetic (top left), potential (top right), and total components (bottom). The phenomenon ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 582.07pt, "of self-interference effects can again be observed; these occur in opposite phase and disappear ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 596.95pt, "after summation. The drop in information from the first to the second plateau is clearly visible, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 611.83pt, "mediated by the negative source term at the right-hand boundary of the layer. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 634.75pt, "What is remarkable about this last example is that all information quantities exhibit a maximum ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 649.63pt, "in the center of the signal, in contrast to the previous examples, where a minimum was present ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 664.54pt, "at the same location. These observations are in complete agreement with the difference wave ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 679.42pt, "fields in Figures 5 and 8, where a similar behavior can be observed. ")
]

