#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.13pt, 790.176pt, "50 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 82.08pt, "Cbits/m. The maximum values amount to 5.2304 Cbits/m for reflection and 0.203 Cbits/m for ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 96.98pt, "transmission. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 119.9pt, "Across all four examples, a total of 112.36 Cbits/m are generated on the reflection side, com-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 134.78pt, "pared to 169.12 Cbits/m on the transmission side. This result underscores the well-known fact ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 149.66pt, "that both measurement setups have their place. While transmission setups are well-suited for ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 164.54pt, "thickness and sound velocity measurements, reflection methods are suitable for density and ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 179.42pt, "position changes, as well as thickness changes. The latter are apparently more difficult to meas-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 194.3pt, "ure than position changes. Density changes are much harder to extract than sound velocity ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 209.18pt, "changes and exhibit the lowest information output of all four examples. If the integrated infor-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 224.06pt, "mation for the density change is normalized to one, the resulting multipliers are 60 for thickness ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 238.94pt, "changes, 1000 for position changes, and 1750 for sound velocity changes. The Cbit values thus ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 253.94pt, "span a range of more than three orders of magnitude. It should be emphasized that these values ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 268.82pt, "are only valid for the specific configuration of the initial model presented here and cannot be ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 284.09pt, "generalized. Since the square of the parameter ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.73pt, 284.09pt, "𝑃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(300.41pt, 284.09pt, " under consideration appears as a scaling factor ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 299.21pt, "in all information-related quantities, the specific choice of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(354.19pt, 299.21pt, "𝑃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(361.87pt, 299.21pt, " has a significant influence on the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 314.09pt, "absolute Cbit values. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.944pt, 359.81pt, "7.")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 359.81pt, "Significance of Information Measure for NDE, SHM, ML and Simulation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 382.73pt, "The information concept presented in this work is so universal and fundamental that it could ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 397.61pt, "have a significant impact on inspection techniques, evaluation methods, and numerical simula-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 412.49pt, "tions. The most important aspects are briefly discussed below. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 458.33pt, "7.1 Nondestructive Evaluation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 481.27pt, "Naturally, not all parameter changes implemented in this work using numerical simulations can ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 496.15pt, "be reproduced in practical testing. Nevertheless, there are several opportunities to modify indi-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 511.03pt, "vidual parameters experimentally. For example, artificially introduced defects in test speci-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 525.91pt, "mens, such as notches or cylindrical boreholes, could be gradually enlarged, and the resulting ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 540.79pt, "information extracted from the difference wave fields. Changes in the position of defects rela-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 555.67pt, "tive to the probes can also be achieved through small adjustments to the probe positions. Local ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 570.55pt, "temperature changes of inclusions could modify their elastic properties, thus enabling material-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 585.43pt, "related parameter changes as well. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 608.35pt, "Furthermore, it is expected that new evaluation methods and imaging algorithms will be devel-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 623.23pt, "oped in the future that directly utilize difference wave fields instead of absolute wave fields. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 638.11pt, "Since the difference signals encode pure information regarding individual parameters, more ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 652.99pt, "customized and accurate evaluation and imaging methods are conceivable. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 698.86pt, "7.2 Structural Health Monitoring ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 721.78pt, "SHM has long used difference wave fields and difference signals to evaluate system changes ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 736.66pt, "relative to an existing baseline. The information concept presented in this work changes the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 751.536pt, "perspective on differential fields and enables a more targeted approach to extracting individual ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 766.416pt, "parameters. Extending the theory to several parameters that change simultaneously and ")
]

