  #line-at(70.944pt, 368.33pt, "almost identical for small parameter changes, each difference field with respect to a specific ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 383.21pt, "parameter differs significantly from the difference fields of the other parameters. Therefore, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 398.21pt, "difference wave fields appear to be much better suited for classification tasks than absolute ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 413.09pt, "wave fields. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 435.89pt, "An even more crucial aspect of the new information measure for machine learning concerns the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 450.77pt, "interplay between parameter space and feature space (Figure 25). Every existing system con-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 465.79pt, "figuration can be viewed as a single point P")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.97pt, 466.75pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.05pt, 465.79pt, " in a generally high-dimensional parameter space, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 480.67pt, "which completely determines the system by means of geometric and material-related parame-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 495.55pt, "ters. Each individual ultrasound measurement on the system links this single point in parameter ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 510.79pt, "space to a time signal or A-scan with ")
