  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(253.25pt, 304.85pt, ". Thus, the more uniform the probabilities of the individ-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 321.29pt, "ual characters in a message, the higher the entropy of the entire message. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 344.21pt, "Shannon himself described his work as a \"mathematical theory\" of communication. It explicitly ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 359.09pt, "excludes semantic, meaning- and knowledge-related aspects - that is, statements about the usa-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 373.97pt, "ble content of transmitted messages and their meaning for the recipient. This means that a mean-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 388.85pt, "ingful message for the recipient can be transmitted just as easily as a completely meaningless, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 403.85pt, "random sequence of characters. Although Shannon's theory is usually referred to as an infor-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 418.73pt, "mation theory, it therefore makes no direct statements about the information content of trans-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 433.61pt, "mitted messages. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 456.53pt, "In contrast, the “change information” presented in this work is different. Here, the occurrence ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 471.43pt, "of large absolute field changes in response to certain relative parameter changes does indeed ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 486.31pt, "represent usable and meaningful information for the receiver or inspector, because it allows the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 501.19pt, "sensitivity of the system, or more precisely, the measurement performed on it, to specific phys-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 516.07pt, "ical parameter changes to be quantified. Against this background, the change information can ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 530.95pt, "be considered not only a mathematical but also a physical information theory. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 553.87pt, "The principles of Shannon theory listed in equations (84) und (85) also have no significant ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 568.75pt, "relevance for the change information or the underlying difference wave fields, since the infor-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 583.63pt, "mation content there does not correlate with the relative frequency of the amplitude values ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 598.51pt, "occurring in the difference signal, but rather with the squared amplitude values or their time ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 613.39pt, "integral. For these reasons, a closer connection between Shannon information and change in-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 628.27pt, "formation cannot be established at this point. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 674.14pt, "8.2 Fisher Information: Information as a Precise Statistical Estimate ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 697.06pt, "Fisher information, named after the British statistician Ronald Fisher, is a measure in mathe-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 711.94pt, "matical statistics that provides information about the best possible quality of parameter esti-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 726.82pt, "mates [5, 6]. It plays an important role in the theory of maximum likelihood estimation and is ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 741.7pt, "also used in Bayesian statistics for calculating prior distributions. Fisher information is a meas-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 756.936pt, "ure of how much information an observable random variable ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
