  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.944pt, 286.25pt, "9.")
  #line-at(106.94pt, 286.25pt, "Summary and Outlook ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 309.17pt, "9.1 Summary ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.944pt, 332.09pt, "In this work, a new information theory for non-destructive ultrasonic testing based on difference ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 346.97pt, "and differential wave fields, respectively, was developed and numerically verified using a sim-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 361.85pt, "plified one-dimensional numerical model. Analogous to Poynting's theorem for energy trans-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 376.73pt, "ported in an ultrasonic field, a balance equation for structural information was derived and suc-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 391.61pt, "cessfully tested for physical plausibility. Key components of this balance equation are the in-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 406.49pt, "formation density as a balance quantity and an information flux vector as the counterpart to the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 421.37pt, "Poynting vector of energy flow. Unlike the energy balance equation, the information balance ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 436.25pt, "includes additional source terms, so that it does not become a continuity equation even after the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 451.13pt, "excitation signal ceases. This contrasts with the statement in [8], where a continuity equation is ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 466.03pt, "assumed for the electromagnetic field. The present work clearly demonstrates that, unlike en-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 481.03pt, "ergy, information in an elastodynamic field is ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(297.29pt, 481.03pt, "not")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(312.77pt, 481.03pt, " a conserved physical quantity. Information ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 495.91pt, "can only be temporarily conserved between two interactions. During the interaction itself, in-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 510.79pt, "formation can be generated as well as annihilated, even if no energy dissipation is inherent in ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 525.67pt, "the system. Generation of information occurs primarily at the interfaces between two materials, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 540.55pt, "but in the case of changes in sound velocity, also within the volume of the changing material. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 555.43pt, "The information propagates from the sources to the sensors, with the ultrasound waves them-")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 570.31pt, "selves acting as information carriers. Information therefore propagates at the speed of sound. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 593.23pt, "The investigations further demonstrated that information, like energy, can be split into kinetic ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 608.11pt, "and potential components. Except for temporary self-interference effects occurring within the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 622.99pt, "model volume, kinetic and potential information exhibit qualitatively and quantitatively similar ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 637.87pt, "behavior, such that the total information essentially results from twice the kinetic or potential ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 652.75pt, "component. While the kinetic component of the information assumes the same mathematical ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 667.66pt, "expression in all the examples considered, the potential component is described by an extended ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 682.54pt, "expression in the case of material-related system parameters that are associated with density ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 697.54pt, "changes. This also applies to the information flux vector. At the stress-free model boundaries, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 712.42pt, "the information is completely given by the kinetic term and therefore assumes a particularly ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 727.3pt, "simple form there, which is proportional to the kinetic energy of the differential wave field. ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 750.456pt, "By appropriately scaling with the system parameter ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.33pt, 750.456pt, "𝑃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(325.01pt, 750.456pt, " under consideration (or its square), which ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 765.336pt, "corresponds to introducing a relative parameter change, and normalizing to the energy of the ")
]

